The function `min_cost` iterates through the cost matrix starting from the second row and second column. For each cell, it updates its value to be the sum of its current value and the minimum value of the three adjacent cells (up, left, or diagonally up-left). This way, it builds up the minimum cost to reach each cell from the starting point (0, 0). Finally, the function returns the value at the destination cell (m, n), which represents the minimum cost of reaching that point from the source.

