To find the largest possible value of k such that k modulo x is y, we can use the following Python code:

```python
def find_max_val(x, y, y_mod_x):
    if x < y:
        return None  # There is no possible value of k in this case
    return y_mod_x + (x - y_mod_x)%(x//y_mod_x)
```

This function takes three parameters: x, y, and y_mod_x. It first checks if x is less than y, in which case it returns None since there is no possible value of k in this case. Otherwise, it calculates the largest possible value of k using the formula y_mod_x + (x - y_mod_x)%(x//y_mod_x),
which effectively increments y_mod_x by the remainder when x is divided by y_mod_x (i.e., x - y_mod_x).
This is because the remainder when x is divided by y_mod_x is k modulo x, and we need to increment k by the remainder to achieve the desired k modulo x.

```python
def find_max_val(x, y, k):
    if k % x == y:
        return k + (x - y)
    else:
        return k - (k % x)
```

