The `lobb_num` function calculates the Lobb number, which is the number of labeled graphs with \( n \) vertices and \( m \) edges. The function uses the logarithm function from the `math` module to compute the contribution of each vertex to the Lobb number. If the vertex index \( i \) is odd, it adds \( \log(i) \times i \) to the result; if even, it subtracts \( \log(i) \times i \) from the result. Finally, the function returns the Lobb number as an integer.

